+## Git Repository and Index Snapshot
+
+[`internal/gitsnap`](internal/gitsnap) captures the live Git state Sections
+10.4 (`kind = git` member) and 12.1-12.3 require: repository identity,
+sanitized remotes, HEAD/ref mode, worktree metadata, index stages and
+flags, staged and unstaged deltas, and tracked file modes. The production
+entry is `Capture`, which drives the Git executable through a `Runner`
+seam (`ExecGitRunner` in production, a scripted fake in tests) with
+`GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, so a capture never takes an index or reference
+lock. `Capture` mutates no durable state: it returns a complete validated
+snapshot or a `*Refusal` naming the registry gate that fired, never a
+partial snapshot.
+
+Sixteen refusal gates cover the scope, each named in `gates.go` with its
+specification clause and driven through `Capture` by its proving test
+(see `gateProvingTests` in `census_test.go`). The gate census counts
+literal `refuse(Gate...)` call sites in non-test production files after
+stripping comments and string literals: 16 of 16 registry rows have at
+least one site, and 3 of 3 refusal codes are live. The census ships
+controls: comment and string-literal plants stay uncounted, an
+unregistered planted gate reddens, and an alias-bound call stays
+invisible, which is the stated blind spot the package upholds by always
+invoking `refuse` directly.
+
+Arithmetic edges are proven at the production entry in both directions:
+remotes accept 16 and refuse 17, index entries accept 65536 and refuse
+65537 with `capability_unavailable`, identity accepts 256 characters and
+refuses 257, stage accepts 3 and refuses 4 (the `TM-GIT-N2` mutation),
+and index version accepts 2-4 while refusing 1 and 5. The identity bound
+counts characters, not bytes: a 256-character multibyte identity
+captures. Repeat captures of a quiesced repository encode
+byte-identically; a HEAD, index, or delta stream that moves mid-capture
+is refused with `workspace_conflict` after a closing re-read, and a
+retry heals. The `WS-GIT-ROUNDTRIP-1` parent and child index lines are
+quoted verbatim from the specification and parsed through `Capture` into
+the normative wire entries.
+
+Stated bounds: object packs, raw index blobs, untracked and ignored
+bytes, symlink targets, submodule recursion, and working-tree manifests
+belong to sibling leaves of the same story and are not produced here;
+the `entry_count` wire-mismatch refusal belongs to
+`internal/canonicaljson`; refusal codes are diagnostic strings in the
+specification vocabulary and are not `axerror` envelopes. Run the
+package gates with:
+
+```bash
+go test ./internal/gitsnap -count=1
+go test ./internal/gitsnap -cover -count=1
+```
+
